#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:5
msgid "内部エネルギー"
msgstr "Internal Energy"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:9
msgid "内部エネルギー（全エネルギー）"
msgstr "Internal Energy (Total Energy)"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:11
msgid "系を構成する要素の運動エネルギーとポテンシャルエネルギーの和"
msgstr ""
"The internal energy is the sum of the kinetic energy and potential energy"
" of the constituents of the system,"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:13
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"U = T_{\\rm kin} + V_{\\rm pot} .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"U = T_{\\rm kin} + V_{\\rm pot} .\n"
"\n"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:17
msgid ""
"であり、力学でエネルギー保存則などを議論するときの、あのエネルギーである。\\ "
"系の「全エネルギー」と呼ぶ事も多い。電子とイオン（または原子核）からなる材料系の場合は"
msgstr ""
"which is the familiar energy of mechanics used in discussions of "
"conservation of energy.\\  It is also often called the total energy of "
"the system. For a material system made up of electrons and ions (or "
"nuclei), it can be written as"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:20
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"U = T_{\\rm ion} + V_{\\rm ion-ion} + T_{\\rm ele} + V_{\\rm ele-ele} + "
"V_{\\rm ele-ion}  ,\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"U = T_{\\rm ion} + V_{\\rm ion-ion} + T_{\\rm ele} + V_{\\rm ele-ele} + "
"V_{\\rm ele-ion}  ,\n"
"\n"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:24
msgid ""
"と書ける。各項の意味は大体察しが付くだろう。\\ :math:`\\rm ele` の添え字を含む後半の３項は電子が関与するため、\\ "
"通常は量子力学的に扱う事が求められる。\\ その場合にはハミルトニアンと呼ばれる演算子"
msgstr ""
"The meaning of each term should be evident. The subscript \\ :math:`\\rm "
"ele` marks the last three terms, which involve electrons\\  and therefore"
" usually require a quantum mechanical treatment.\\  In that case, we "
"define an operator called the Hamiltonian,"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:29
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\hat{H}\n"
"\\equiv\n"
"\\hat{T}_{\\rm ele} + \\hat{V}_{\\rm ele-ele} + \\hat{V}_{\\rm ele-ion} ,"
"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\hat{H}\n"
"\\equiv\n"
"\\hat{T}_{\\rm ele} + \\hat{V}_{\\rm ele-ele} + \\hat{V}_{\\rm ele-ion} ,"
"\n"
"\n"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:35
msgid "を定義し、これの期待値を計算する。電子系の温度依存性をまともに考慮する場合は"
msgstr ""
"and calculate its expectation value. To account explicitly for the "
"temperature dependence of the electronic system, we calculate"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:37
msgid ""
"\\left< \\hat{H} \\right>\n"
"=\n"
"\\frac{Tr\\left(\\hat{H}e^{-\\beta\\hat{H}}\\right)}{Tr\\left(e^{-\\beta\\hat{H}}\\right)}"
"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\left< \\hat{H} \\right>\n"
"=\n"
"\\frac{Tr\\left(\\hat{H}e^{-\\beta\\hat{H}}\\right)}{Tr\\left(e^{-\\beta\\hat{H}}\\right)}"
"\n"
"\n"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:43
msgid "という計算を行う事になるが、多くの場合はSchrödinger方程式"
msgstr "In most cases, however, we instead use the Schrödinger equation"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:45
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\hat{H} \\Phi_{\\rm n} = E_{\\rm n} \\Phi_{\\rm n}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\\hat{H} \\Phi_{\\rm n} = E_{\\rm n} \\Phi_{\\rm n}\n"
"\n"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:49
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"の基底状態のエネルギー固有値 :math:`E_0` を用いる。\\ これは電子系の第一励起状態のエネルギー（バンドギャップなど）が eV "
"のオーダーで離れていればかなり良い近似だと考えられる。\\ 通常、多電子系のSchrödinger方程式 :eq:`inte5` "
"は、基底状態に対しても容易には解けないため、\\ 実用的には、密度汎関数法（DFT = Density Functional "
"Theory）等を用いて基底状態エネルギーの計算が行われる。\\ DFTに基づく第一原理計算ソフトでは :eq:`inte2` の "
":math:`V_{\\rm ion-ion}` まで含め、\\ イオンの座標（まとめて :math:`\\boldsymbol{R}_{\\rm"
" ion}` と記すことにする）を与えれば\\ 確定する成分、すなわちイオンのポテンシャルエネルギーと解釈できる部分を全エネルギー\\ "
"として出力するものが多い。以上を踏まえて :eq:`inte2` を書き直すと、"
msgstr ""
"and take its ground-state energy eigenvalue :math:`E_0`.\\  This is "
"expected to be a fairly good approximation if the first excited state of "
"the electrons lies on the order of 1 eV above the ground state (for "
"example, across a band gap).\\  Because the many-electron Schrödinger "
"equation, Equation :eq:`inte5`, is usually difficult to solve even for "
"the ground state,\\  in practice the ground-state energy is calculated "
"using methods such as density functional theory (DFT).\\  Many DFT-based "
"first-principles codes add to the electronic terms of Equation "
":eq:`inte2` the term :math:`V_{\\rm ion-ion}` as well.\\  The resulting "
"energy is fixed once the ionic coordinates (denoted collectively by "
":math:`\\boldsymbol{R}_{\\rm ion}`) are specified,\\  so it can be "
"interpreted as the potential energy of the ions, and these codes report "
"it\\  as the total energy. With this in mind, we can rewrite Equation "
":eq:`inte2` as"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:58
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"U = T_{\\rm ion} + E_{\\rm DFT}\\left(\\boldsymbol{R}_{\\rm ion}\\right)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"U = T_{\\rm ion} + E_{\\rm DFT}\\left(\\boldsymbol{R}_{\\rm ion}\\right)\n"
"\n"

#: ../../thermo/internal_energy.rst:62
msgid "と書けて、これが :eq:`inte1` 式に対応するものとなる。"
msgstr "This is the counterpart of Equation :eq:`inte1`."

